  "pages": [
    {
      "cover": true,
      "sentenceId": 0,
      "image": "assets/images/00.webp",
      "audio": "",
      "en": "",
      "cn": ""
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s43-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p01.mp3",
      "en": "After it rains, we put away our umbrellas.",
      "cn": "雨停之后，我们收起雨伞。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s43-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p02.mp3",
      "en": "Then we may see rainbows in the sky above us.",
      "cn": "这时，在头顶上方的天空中，我们可能会看到彩虹。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s43-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p03.mp3",
      "en": "The conditions need to be just right to see a rainbow.",
      "cn": "要看到彩虹，必须有恰到好处的条件。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s43-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p04.mp3",
      "en": "We need some water drops in the air, like rain, fog or clouds.",
      "cn": "我们需要空气中有一些水滴，比如雨、雾或云。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s43-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p05.mp3",
      "en": "And we need the sun to be behind us and low to the ground, which often happens in the autumn.",
      "cn": "同时需要太阳位于我们身后且位置较低，这种情况在秋季经常出现。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s43-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p06.mp3",
      "en": "Because a rainbow is created by light passing through water drops.",
      "cn": "因为彩虹是由光线穿过水滴形成的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s43-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p07.mp3",
      "en": "As the name suggests, rainbows are supposed to be the shape of a bow.",
      "cn": "顾名思义，彩虹（rainbow）应该呈弓（bow）形。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s43-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p08.mp3",
      "en": "Neither the sun nor the water drops are the same every time, so each rainbow is unique.",
      "cn": "每次的太阳和水滴都不会是一模一样的，所以每条彩虹都是独一无二的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s43-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p09.mp3",
      "en": "Rainbows could also look like some colourful smoke.",
      "cn": "彩虹也可能看起来像一些彩色的烟雾。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s43-p10-01",
      "image": "assets/images/10.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p10-01.mp3",
      "en": "The light that comes from the sun seems white to us,",
      "cn": "我们看到的来自太阳的光似乎是白色的，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s43-p10-02",
      "image": "assets/images/10.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p10-02.mp3",
      "en": "but the white light is actually a mix of different colours.",
      "cn": "但这种白光实际上是不同颜色混合起来形成的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s43-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p11.mp3",
      "en": "When the light goes through a raindrop, these colours can separate out.",
      "cn": "当光穿过雨滴时，这些颜色就会分离出来。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s43-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p12.mp3",
      "en": "Raindrops look like little balls.",
      "cn": "雨滴看起来像一个个小球。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s43-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p13.mp3",
      "en": "When light hits one of these little balls, it changes direction.",
      "cn": "当光线射到其中一个小球上时，它会改变方向。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s43-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p14.mp3",
      "en": "We call this refraction.",
      "cn": "我们称之为“折射”。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s43-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p15.mp3",
      "en": "Lights of different wavelengths are refracted differently, so they are separated out into different colours.",
      "cn": "不同波长的光折射程度不同，因此会被分离成不同的颜色。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s43-p16",
      "image": "assets/images/16.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p16.mp3",
      "en": "In a rainbow, there are seven colours arranged in a row: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet.",
      "cn": "在彩虹中，有七种颜色依次排列：红、橙、黄、绿、蓝、靛、紫。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s43-p17",
      "image": "assets/images/17.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p17.mp3",
      "en": "While colours like brown and pink are not usually seen.",
      "cn": "而像棕色和粉色等颜色通常是看不到的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s43-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p18.mp3",
      "en": "And we would never see black and white in a rainbow.",
      "cn": "我们永远不会在彩虹中看到黑色和白色。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 20,
      "sourceSentenceId": 19,
      "chunkId": "s43-p19",
      "image": "assets/images/19.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p19.mp3",
      "en": "Black is what we see when there's no light, while white is a mix of all the colours together.",
      "cn": "黑色是在没有光的情况下我们看到的颜色，而白色则是所有颜色的混合。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 21,
      "sourceSentenceId": 20,
      "chunkId": "s43-p20",
      "image": "assets/images/20.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p20.mp3",
      "en": "The science of rainbows is fascinating.",
      "cn": "彩虹的科学原理非常迷人。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 22,
      "sourceSentenceId": 21,
      "chunkId": "s43-p21",
      "image": "assets/images/21.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p21.mp3",
      "en": "Even on a busy weekday, we should look up to the sky.",
      "cn": "即使在忙碌的工作日，我们也应该抬头看看天空。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 23,
      "sourceSentenceId": 22,
      "chunkId": "s43-p22",
      "image": "assets/images/22.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p22.mp3",
      "en": "It's an easy way to appreciate the beauty of nature.",
      "cn": "这是欣赏自然之美的一种简单方式。"
    }
  ]
}
